SUMMARY:ABCD Reads Exit Party by Emily St. John Mandel
DESCRIPTION:A Book Club\, Downtown (ABCD)\nABCD Reads ***[Exit Party](http
 s://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/record/S234C4792123)*** by Emily St. John Man
 del (author of ***Station Eleven***).\n([RESULTS](https://opavote.com/resu
 lts/5182568441053184) of the poll for this event.)\n\n**:: ABOUT THE BOOK 
 ::**\n"From the bestselling author of Station Eleven\, Exit Party is Emily
  St. John Mandel’s epic new story of crimes committed and loves lost acr
 oss worlds and decades.\n2031\\. America is at war with itself\\\, but for
  the first time in weeks there is some hope: the Republic of California ha
 s been declared\\\, the curfew in Los Angeles is lifted\\\, and everyone i
 n the city is going to a party\\.\nAri\, newly released from prison\, arri
 ves with her friend Gloria just as a fragile new era begins. But there are
  people at the party who shouldn’t be there. Something is very wrong...\
 nYears later\, living a different life in Paris\, Ari remains haunted by t
 hat night. Whatever happened at the party fractured her sense of reality 
 – and may hold the key to a very different world.\nFreedom and surveilla
 nce\, art and survival\, love and loss in a broken world: Exit Party is th
 e electrifying new novel from Emily St. John Mandel." (from [Goodreads](ht
 tps://www.goodreads.com/book/show/241683548-exit-party?ac=1&from_search=tr
 ue&qid=8V5Hrtzu0U&rank=1))\n\n"A novel of doubles\, shadow worlds\, and fr
 actured timelines as a man disappears from a glittering Los Angeles party\
 , and a woman—a gunrunner\, an art collector\, an operative of the State
 —searches for answers." (from [BookMarks.reviews](https://bookmarks.revi
 ews/reviews/exit-party/))\n\n**:: ABOUT THE EVENT ::**\nYou are welcome to
  arrive 30 minutes before the event and stay 30 minutes or longer afterwar
 d to connect with other attendees outside the book talk.\n\nPlease ensure 
 you have read the book before attending (though finishing any book is not 
 a barrier to participating\, as long as you don't mind spoilers).\n\nFirst
 -time attendees can join for free. If the event is full\, we maintain an u
 nofficial waitlist. Please send [Michael](https://www.meetup.com/members/5
 5295192/) a direct message for more information\, in either case.\n\nWe re
 quest a $3 contribution from regular attendees to help cover our monthly m
 eetup costs.\n\n**:: ABOUT OUR NEXT BOOK ::**\nAt the end of each event\, 
 we will ask for nominees for our next book. If you have a good one in mind
 \, please ensure it is between 200-400 pages long\, available from the Tor
 onto Public Library\, and counts as contemporary literary fiction (though 
 these are not hard and fast rules). When enough nominees are collected\, M
 ichael will send the members a direct message with a link where you can vo
 te.
